From: crosshatch-player <dlab-g3@local>
Subject: [PATCH] Read the buffer again before copying a PLTE or tRNS that runs past it

PNGdec 1.1.6 copies a PLTE (into its 1,024-byte palette) and a tRNS (into the
palette's alpha) straight out of its 2 KiB file buffer, without checking that
the chunk's data is all in it: an indexed PNG with 1.3 to 2 KB of iCCP or tEXt
before its palette makes the copy read past the PNG object. This refuses a
PLTE over 768 bytes or a tRNS over 256 (more than the palette holds), and
reads the buffer again from the chunk's data when it runs past the bytes read.
The display lab's PNGdec patch, the x4pro env only: applied by
scripts/patch_lab_decoders.py and by test/game_display_lab/CMakeLists.txt (the
host decoder tests, on a copy). Other envs keep PNGdec as released; the fix
is a suggestion for upstream.

---
--- a/src/png.inl
+++ b/src/png.inl
@@ -832,6 +832,26 @@
         }
         iMarker = MOTOLONG(&s[iOffset+4]);
         iOffset += 8; // point to the marker data
+        // CrossPoint patch: PLTE and tRNS are copied out of the file buffer below, which a chunk that starts near the
+        // buffer's end runs past (the copy then reads past this object). Refuse one larger than the palette holds,
+        // and read the buffer again from the chunk's data when it is not all in it.
+        if (iMarker == 0x504c5445 || iMarker == 0x74524e53) {
+            if (iLen > (iMarker == 0x504c5445 ? 768 : 256)) {
+                pPage->iError = PNG_DECODE_ERROR;
+                return 1;
+            }
+            if (iOffset + iLen > iBytesRead) {
+                iFileOffset += (iOffset - iBytesRead); // the chunk's data, in the file
+                (*pPage->pfnSeek)(&pPage->PNGFile, iFileOffset);
+                iBytesRead = (*pPage->pfnRead)(&pPage->PNGFile, s, PNG_FILE_BUF_SIZE);
+                if (iBytesRead < iLen) {
+                    pPage->iError = PNG_DECODE_ERROR;
+                    return 1;
+                }
+                iFileOffset += iBytesRead;
+                iOffset = 0;
+            }
+        }
         switch (iMarker)
         {
             case 0x44474b62: // 'bKGD' DEBUG
